  "scope": "Reference audited-cancellation decisions and write ordering for borrowed in-memory state and a single consumed native SQLite transaction, after native durable admission and encoding.",
  "limitations": [
    "The frozen policy shares native storage, row decoding, input admission, codecs, cancellation and group finalization primitives. It is not independent persistence or complete host-neutral recovery.",
    "Memory cancellation retains existing partial mutation semantics when its native finalization fails; audit insertion follows successful cancellation. No transactional rollback is claimed for memory.",
    "Disposable corruption fixtures restore foreign-key/check enforcement before invoking the native cancellation transaction. They are not valid arbitrary saved-frame import examples.",
    "SQLite failures cover audit insertion, terminal/dispatch/group writes and deferred constraint failure at commit. Quota callback failure and native unwinds are direct adapter tests, not physical disk-full or power-loss testing.",
    "The transaction and memory hooks remain trusted native owners, not debugger authorization grants. Native record reading/decoding and ordinary cancellation remain separate work.",
    "No new Linux, remote CI, live GUI, standalone exported-source execution, physical multi-host or throughput benchmark is claimed."
  ],
